  "finding": "Adding 1.2 seconds before the virtual passkey call did not reduce median respond latency in this small control. A delayed sample still waited740ms in B input-bound admission, while setup preparation had already been admitted.",
  "limits": [
    "Four samples per group cannot characterize tail latency or rule out a benefit for other pending-preparation cases.",
    "The delay changes preparation lead time and request timing. It is a diagnostic intervention, not a performance fix or a real Touch ID measurement.",
    "Actual authentication-stage durations still vary and are reported for every sample.",
    "Role logs are joined by exact public protocol-session key, then object ID across events. No time-window join is used.",
    "Root wait is nested in admission bind; peer preparation and role execution overlap. Do not add those durations.",
    "The 740ms input-bound admission call does not identify how much time was transport, durable acknowledgement, queueing, or execution. Original long preparation stall was not reproduced."
  ],
